}A & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 \\\\ -4 & -3\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+\\frac{4}{3}{R}_{1}\\,⟺\\,\\overset{{E}_{1}}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ \\frac{4}{3} & 1\\end{aligned}]}}\\cdot A \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -\\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =U\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe reduced matrix is upper triangular, so it is our matrix $U.$ Now, since ${E}_{1}A=U,$ we can invert ${E}_{1}$ to arrive at the desired LU factorization:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{E}_{1}A & =U \\\\ A & ={E}_{1}^{-1}U \\\\ A & ={[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ \\frac{4}{3} & 1\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}U \\\\ A & ={{[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -\\frac{4}{3} & 1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{L}{{[\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -\\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{U}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-8e1d1148-bcd2-52a8-8f81-b71b67b2ffca"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-8e1d1148-bcd2-52a8-8f81-b71b67b2ffca" :answer-field/id #uuid "8e1d1148-bcd2-52a8-8f81-b71b67b2ffca" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-c590c844-2750-5967-9186-1929bef3ad9d" :answer-field/choices ["answer-32a6d60c-f610-5c43-93e3-26b4c7b8c43a" "answer-c590c844-2750-5967-9186-1929bef3ad9d" "answer-c1e9051f-1d37-5262-a9e6-23f05619b3f7" "answer-4181c1fa-946f-565a-866c-52fd5708af44" "answer-cb607a13-8642-5e1f-a387-54eb7ab5bef0"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-32a6d60c-f610-5c43-93e3-26b4c7b8c43a" :answer/id #uuid "32a6d60c-f610-5c43-93e3-26b4c7b8c43a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{4}{3} & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c590c844-2750-5967-9186-1929bef3ad9d" :answer/id #uuid "c590c844-2750-5967-9186-1929bef3ad9d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -\\frac{4}{3} & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "a