 decomposition $A=LU,$ then $L=$"] ["question-903883c2-c07e-50f2-a202-1c38e08cadfc" :question/worked-solution "To find the matrices $L$ and $U,$ we reduce the matrix $A$ to row echelon form. Whilst doing this, we simultaneously write down the row operations applied to $A$ in terms of matrix multiplication using elementary matrices:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ -5 & 6\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+5{R}_{1}\\,⟺\\,\\overset{{E}_{1}}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 5 & 1\\end{aligned}]}}\\cdot A \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =U\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe reduced matrix is upper triangular, so it is our matrix $U.$ Now, since ${E}_{1}A=U,$ we can invert ${E}_{1}$ to arrive at the desired LU factorization:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{E}_{1}A & =U \\\\ A & ={E}_{1}^{-1}U \\\\ A & ={[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 5 & 1\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}U \\\\ A & ={{[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -5 & 1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{L}{{[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -4\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{U}\\end{aligned}\n$$"] ["question-903883c2-c07e-50f2-a202-1c38e08cadfc" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy] ["answer-field-808d2fc9-2e7f-5ef1-86ff-cfcf9e8e2abc" :answer-field/id #uuid "808d2fc9-2e7f-5ef1-86ff-cfcf9e8e2abc"] ["answer-d132d4d7-ae01-5ea2-9daa-327961d8af0a" :answer/id #uuid "d132d4d7-ae01-5ea2-9daa-327961d8af0a"] ["answer-d132d4d7-ae01-5ea2-9daa-327961d8af0a" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-d132d4d7-ae01-5ea2-9daa-327961d8af0a" :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-5 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]"] ["answer-4f40f169-2bde-5c99-911f-380da9f1b008" :answer/id #uuid "4f40f169-2bde-5c99-911f-380da9f1b008"] ["answer-4f40f169-2bde-5c99-911f-380da9f1b008" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-4f40f169-2bde-5c99-911f-380da9f1b008" :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}]"] ["answer-5d903dcf-e2e4-575c-918f-1685ca2aa827" :answer/id #uuid "5d903dcf-e2e4-575c-918f-1685ca2aa827"] ["answer-5d903dcf